        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Hours.</strong> A coordinator covers a shift. Tenant emergencies, and the pre-semester showing rush, do not stay inside that shift. Nights, weekends, sick days, and the hour they are on a showing in Rogers while a pipe fails in Fayetteville are the gap.</li>
          <li><strong>The job that remains.</strong> Vendor relationships, owner reporting, and the angry or unusual call still need a person who knows the portfolio. This does not replace that person. It keeps the phone from being the reason they cannot do the rest of the work.</li>
          <li><strong>Published prices, not estimates we wrote for this page.</strong> Our price next to named answering vendors, and the receptionist wage comparison we will actually stand behind, is on the <a class="text-link" href="/learn/ai-receptionist-cost/">AI receptionist cost page</a>. If your volume is low and you only need a human to take messages during the day, say so on the assessment. We will tell you if you should not buy this.</li>
        </ul>

